WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 9.2 · Financial Management
The organisational budget

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Budget your whole first year from real prices, and plan what you will cut if income falls short.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.022
An organisational budget estimates all your income and spending for the year ahead. It is a plan for the whole initiative, not just the part a funder or first customer will pay for.

4
00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:28.022
Three parts of the budget

5
00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:39.352
Expenditure: Every cost: services, people, premises, equipment, insurance, fees and a contribution to reserves. For example: The youth club lists hall hire, insurance, snacks, a laptop and registration fees.

6
00:00:39.352 --> 00:00:51.052
Income, by certainty: Each source marked confirmed, likely or possible, so you see how solid your plan is. For example: Membership fees confirmed, a local grant likely, a crowdfunding campaign only possible.

7
00:00:51.052 --> 00:01:05.804
Contingency and cuts: A buffer for higher costs, and a plan for what you cut if income does not arrive. For example: If the grant fails, the club drops the summer trip and keeps its weekly sessions.

8
00:01:06.204 --> 00:01:06.804
Why it matters now

9
00:01:06.804 --> 00:01:12.848
1. You have no past spending, so written assumptions are your only guide.

10
00:01:12.848 --> 00:01:19.263
2. It shows the full cost of your plan, not just one funded part.

11
00:01:19.263 --> 00:01:25.567
3. It lets you compare your plan with reality every month.

12
00:01:25.967 --> 00:01:26.567
What it guides

13
00:01:26.567 --> 00:01:31.870
1. Your project budgets, which must add up to this one.

14
00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:37.174
2. Your cash flow forecast and your monthly budget versus actual.

15
00:01:37.174 --> 00:01:43.107
3. Your prices and funding asks, based on real costs.

16
00:01:43.507 --> 00:01:44.107
What to avoid

17
00:01:44.107 --> 00:01:49.041
Guessing costs instead of getting quotes and real prices.

18
00:01:49.041 --> 00:01:54.344
Planning spending against possible income with no plan to cut.

19
00:01:54.344 --> 00:02:00.648
Leaving out founder pay, insurance, fees or a contingency line.

20
00:02:01.248 --> 00:02:03.048
You write your first-year budget headings and assumptions.

21
00:02:03.048 --> 00:02:07.048
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:08.548 --> 00:02:11.648
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
